ifting EU shared tenant worker pools, which directly overlaps the PR 842 canary cohort.\n* **Next Useful Actions:** Preserve the existing request identity [`record-54bad5e8e1`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-54bad5e8e1.md) without issuing duplicate releases; track the operation until actual canary deployment and exposure are confirmed; coordinate cohort separation with `routing-quality`; and conduct post-exposure canary observation against the baseline.\n\nPlease inspect the full analysis, source paths, and evidence IDs in [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).","thinking":"**Reviewing Task & Context**\n\nThe request involves a handoff review using a specified skill definition and monitoring a queue retry fix post-PR 842, specifically addressing a timeout report and previous handoff suggestions about potentially closing the monitor. The aim is to reconstruct the system's actual state and determine the appropriate course of action. The product workspace contains relevant documentation to begin the investigation.\n\n\n"}
